turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** Appointing a principal underwriter on a series-trust platform (e.g., the distributor affiliated with Foreside/ACA, Quasar, Northern Lights) is mainly a **legal and operational role**. The underwriter is the FINRA-registered broker-dealer named under the trust's distribution agreement. It reviews marketing materials for compliance (FINRA Rule 2210), handles the paperwork for authorized-participant creation and redemption orders, and supports registration obligations. It does **not**, by itself, provide wholesalers, a sales force, or asset inflows.\n\n**Asset gathering is usually contracted separately.** It may come from:\n- the adviser's own sales team\n- third-party marketing or wholesaling firms\n- paid platform or \"shelf\" access agreements and revenue-sharing with intermediaries such as wirehouses, RIA custodians and model marketplaces\n- capital-markets and lead-market-maker support\n\n**Packages differ.** Some white-label providers bundle distribution, marketing and capital-markets help, often for extra fees. Others are compliance-only. Sponsors should check the contracts and fee schedules for what is actually provided. Approval on intermediary platforms and flows remain the adviser's job.","ttft_ms":1729,"type":"result","duration_ms":6494,"uuid":"7c6fc2fd-c47f-437f-900c-3a7359db4527","ttft_stream_ms":1646,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1646,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
